Where do I download the  DNABERT-2 documents


Everything is in two official places, plus the paper:

Code and benchmark
The official repository is MAGICS-LAB/DNABERT_2 on GitHub (ICLR 2024 paper). It contains the model implementation, the Genome Understanding Evaluation (GUE) benchmark — 28 datasets across species — and the fine-tuning and pre-training scripts (GitHub). To get it:

bash
git clone https://github.com/MAGICS-LAB/DNABERT_2.git
Model weights and tokenizer
The pre-trained checkpoint lives on Hugging Face as zhihan1996/DNABERT-2-117M — 117M parameters, ~470 MB. You don't need to download files manually; transformers fetches them on first use:

python
from transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModel
tok = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained("zhihan1996/DNABERT-2-117M", trust_remote_code=True)
model = AutoModel.from_pretrained("zhihan1996/DNABERT-2-117M", trust_remote_code=True)
For a manual download (the direct file links are in the repo README), grab pytorch_model.bin, config.json, tokenizer.json, and the bert_layers.py/bert_padding.py/flash_attn_triton.py code files from the model page, or use the CLI:

bash
pip install -U "huggingface_hub[cli]"
hf download zhihan1996/DNABERT-2-117M --local-dir dnabert2
Paper
Zhou et al., "DNABERT-2: Efficient Foundation Model and Benchmark for Multi-Species Genome," arXiv:2306.15006 (ICLR 2024).

Two practical notes from my Phase 2 run. First, trust_remote_code=True is required because the attention implementation is custom. Second, if you run it with current library versions you'll likely hit the same three incompatibilities I patched (missing pad_token_id on the config, the ALiBi tensor built during meta-device init, and the GPU-only triton attention branch on CPU) — all documented in the Phase 2 report with exact fixes, so you won't have to rediscover them.

